    "source_excerpt": "Very high doses of ondansetron can affect heart rhythm. In rare cases, this can cause a serious irregular heartbeat called Torsades de Pointes. This risk is for the woman taking ondansetron, not the fetus. If you are taking ondansetron, talk to your healthcare provider about your dose and whether you need any heart monitoring."
